In this Act, unless the context otherwise requires Interpretation "Game Officer" means any officer appointed under section 3 to be Chief Game Warden, Deputy Chief Game Warden, a Game Warden or a Game Ranger; "State Land" has the meaning assigned to it by the Cap. 40 Land Code; "hunt", "kill", "capture", mean hunting killing or capturing by any method, and includes attempts to kill or capture and the taking or disturbing of nests or eggs; "protected animal" means any animal specified in the First Schedule; "shoot" includes shooting at; "trophy" means the head, horn, tooth, tusk, bore, claw, hoof, skin, hair, feather, egg or any durable portion of any animal or the nest of any animal. B.L.R.O. 111984 Appointment 3. (1) His Majesty the Sultan and Yang Di-Pertuan of Chief may appoint a Chief Game Warden, a Deputy Chief Game Game Warden and other Warden and such number of Game Wardens, Game Ranofficers gers and other officers as he may consider necessary for the carrying out of the provision of this Act.

(2) All such officers when appointed shall be subject to the direction of the Chief Game Warden.

WILD LIFE SANCTUARIES Wild Life 4. (1) His Majesty in Council may from time to time Sanctuaries by order published in the Gazette declare any area in Brunei and acts prohibited specified in such declaration to be a Wild Life Sanctuary therein exclusively reserved for the preservation of animals or birds, and may define or alter the limits of any such area.

(2) Subject to the provisions of section 6, no person shall in a Wild Life Sanctuary

(a) sho9t, hunt, kill, capture or take any animal, bird, fish or reptile or take or disturb the nest or eggs of any bird;

(b) keep or carry any weapon or contrivance of any kind used for the taking, shooting, or killing of any animal, bird; fish or reptile;

(c) be in possession of the trophy or flesh of any mammal, bird, fish or reptile;

(d) cut or remove any vegetable;

(e) quarry stone, burn lime or charcoal, or search for, collect or remove any forest produce or minerals;

(f) erect any building, or clear or break up any land for cultivation or for any other purpose; or

(g) kindle, keep or carry any fire or leave any fire burning.

(3) Whoever does any act in contravention of paragraph (a) of subsection (2) shall be guilty of an offence: Penalty, imprisonment for one year and a fine of $2,000. ( 4) Whoever does any act in contravention of paragraph (b), (c), (d), (e), (f) or (g) of subsection (2) shall be guilty of an offence: Penalty, imprisonment for 6 months and a fine of $1,000. ·'

(5) Nothing in this section shall be deemed to prohibit or render punishable any act done with the permission in writing of the Chief Game Warden.

Where, in any proceedings under this Act, any fine is imposed, the court may award any sum or sums not exceeding one-half the total fine collected to any informer or informers: Reward for Provided that no such sum may be awarded to any police informers officer or to any person appointed to assist in the administration of this Act.

PARTY

SCHEDULES AND RULES Power to 25. ( 1) His Majesty in Council may make rules generally make rules for carrying out the provision of this Act, and, in particular, and orders such rules may provide for:

(a) a close season for any kind of wild life;

(b) maturity standards for taking, hunting, killing or capturing any kind of wild life;

(c) controlling the keeping of any kind of wild life in captivity;

(d) controlling the import or export of wild life;

(e) the type of weapons, instruments and contrivances which n1ay be used in taking, shooting or killing of wild life; (/) granting exemption from anything provided by such rules;

(g) appeal against or review of the exercise of any discretion vested by the rules in any Game Officer; and

(h) anything which requires to be provided for by the rule.

(2) His Majesty in Council may, by order signified in the Gazette, amend any of the Schedules.

